Package: CellEvoTree
Type: Package
Title: Phylogeny-Inspired Cell State Evolution Trees
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("YOUR_GIVEN_NAME", "YOUR_FAMILY_NAME", email = "YOUR_EMAIL@example.org", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Builds phylogeny-inspired cell state evolution trees from single-cell
    data. The expression-first workflow uses scalable metacells, gene expression,
    and TF messenger RNA expression to propose primary sister relationships. It
    estimates primary-layer weights and uncertainty by split-feature resampling,
    then audits candidate primary layers using feature reliability, whole-sample
    topology retention, and within-group sample-neighbor enrichment. Audits can
    warn, downweight, or demote unstable optional layers while protecting the
    expression reference geometry. Repeated distance-correlation and local-neighbor
    overlap analyses quantify whether regulon evidence is only partially redundant
    with expression. The workflow then allows regulon and module information to
    refine only topology changes
    that preserve empirical primary-distance, neighborhood, and protected-split
    constraints. Cell-type labels are annotation-only by default and are not
    used for primary distances or topology selection. Slingshot, RNA velocity,
    UMAP, and optional CellRank transition
    priors provide direction and post-hoc biological diagnostics. Sample-aware
    leave-one-sample-out topology stability, per-edge Slingshot and velocity
    direction support, exact Shapley branch-discrimination attribution, and
    multi-start constrained topology search provide explicit uncertainty and
    sensitivity analyses. A known-truth stress benchmark simulates multiple
    topology shapes, cell counts, dropout, sample-batch effects, RNA-velocity
    errors, regulon-edge corruption, and branch drivers. Adaptive batch
    correction combines within-group sample-label permutations with
    empirical-Bayes offset shrinkage. Publication-oriented benchmarks run
    Slingshot and Monocle3 through a common graph-distance interface, accept
    independent reference simulations, report method failures, and perform
    paired bootstrap and multiple-testing-adjusted comparisons. A
    resource-planned topology optimizer reuses topology distances and cached
    reference ranks while retaining exact primary constraints. State-specific
    GRN inference uses SCENIC edge priors with either activity-target products
    or local ridge regression, and known-truth benchmarks evaluate edge gain,
    loss, strengthening, and weakening. Branch Shapley validation can equalize
    biological samples and calibrate attribution with label permutations. A legacy
    balanced multi-view workflow remains available. The package explains branch
    splits and estimates view contributions. Sample-aware metacell boundaries,
    within-group primary-feature centering, and conditional sample-neighbor
    diagnostics support explicit batch-sensitivity analysis. RNA-velocity root
    scores and inverse velocity pseudotime are combined as robust root evidence;
    a weighted tree-median edge orients the tree without requiring a stage label
    to form a monophyletic outgroup. These trees are regulatory
    cell-state trees, not true genetic lineage or mutation-based phylogenies.
